{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Working Hard"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "All in a Day's Work"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.  Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reckon"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bthink or \u200bbelieve"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I reckon that you've had a hard week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are the words to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pull your weight"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do your part"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My team told my editor that I wasn't pulling my weight."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pick up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to learn something quickly and easily"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I suppose I've been a bit slow but I've been trying hard to pick things up! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "training"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the \u200bprocess of \u200blearning the \u200bskills you need to do a \u200bparticular \u200bjob or \u200bactivity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The training that I received wasn't great. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pitch in "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bstart to do something as \u200bpart of a \u200bgroup, \u200bespecially something \u200bhelpful"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You've got to offer to pitch in wherever you can. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get in over one's head "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get involved in a difficult situation that you can't get out of"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I just don't want to get in over my head."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le09ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect with Report or Comment Phrases"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about past events that have a connection to the future. </br> You can use the Present Perfect tense with other verbs to report or comment on events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use verbs such as <span class=\"italic\">reckon</span>, <span class=\"italic\">understand</span>, <span class=\"italic\">suppose</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> guess</span> and <span class=\"italic\">imagine </span>to communicate your thoughts and to report about something that happened in the past and has a connection to the present. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is: </br></br>For example:</br></br><span class=\"italic\"> I<span class=\"strong\"> understand (that) you have done</span> a lot of editing in previous jobs.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I reckon that you've had a hard week."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I suppose I've been a bit slow but I've been trying hard to pick things up! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I understand that you've been put with one of the best teams."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I imagine you've worked hard at the tasks you've been given but you should do more than just the minimum. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Relative Clauses and Adverbial Phrases"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use relative clauses to make your writing and speaking more detailed and sophisticated. A defining clause gives essential information about a noun. A non-defining clause gives additional information about a noun."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In relative clauses, you use <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things, <span class=\"italic\">when</span> with time and <span class=\"italic\">where </span>with places.</br></br>   <span class=\"underline\">Defining Clause:</span></br></br><span class=\"italic\">  People <span class=\"strong\">who talk too much </span>annoy me a lot.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Without the clause \u201cwho talk too much\u201d, the meaning of the sentence changes:  <span class=\"italic\"></br>People annoy me a lot.</span></br></br>   <span class=\"underline\">Non-defining Clause:</span></br></br><span class=\"italic\">  My younger sister, <span class=\"strong\">who is really shy</span>, rarely speaks to anyone.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Without the clause \u201cwho is really shy\u201d the main idea of the sentence stays the same. </br> You use commas to separate the non-defining clause from the rest of the sentence.  </br></br>An adverbial clause is a group of words which plays the role of an adverb. There are different types of adverbial clauses:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbial Clauses of Time </span></br>An adverb of time states when something happens or how often. An adverb of time often starts with one of the following <span class=\"underline\">subordinating conjunctions</span>: <span class=\"italic\">after</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as long as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as soon as</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> before</span>, <span class=\"italic\">no sooner than</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> since</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> until</span>, <span class=\"italic\">when</span>,<span class=\"italic\"></span> or<span class=\"italic\"> while.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbial Clauses of Place</span></br> An adverb of place states where something happens. An adverb of place often starts with a preposition (e.g., <span class=\"italic\">in</span>, <span class=\"italic\">on</span>, <span class=\"italic\">near</span>) or one of the following subordinating conjunctions: <span class=\"italic\"> anywhere</span>, <span class=\"italic\">everywhere</span>, <span class=\"italic\">where</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">wherever</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbial Clauses of Manner</span></br> An adverb of manner states how something is done. An adverb of manner often starts with one of the following subordinating conjunctions:<span class=\"italic\"> as</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> like</span>, <span class=\"italic\"></span>or <span class=\"italic\">the way</span>. </br></br>  Look at some examples from the dialogue:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I hope that your week was better than mine."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have been working hard ever since I got here. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've done everything that I've been asked to do. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The people who I work with haven't been particularly helpful either."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The training that I received wasn't great."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You've got to offer to pitch in wherever you can. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I describe a bad week at work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about problems at work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask for suggestions from a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give advice and suggestions to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a piece of paper, write down five things that happened to make this a very bad week at work. (You can invent these issues, or you can use Adam's bad week)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Have a conversation with a partner and tell them about your bad week at work. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask your partner for some suggestions on how to make next week better."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Switch roles. Listen to your partner talk about their bad week and give them some advice."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le09ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le09ob11re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le09ob11re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Wow, I'm glad that week is over! I hope that your week was better than mine.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: It was good! I reckon that you've had a hard week. What happened?<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Well, apparently my team told my editor that I wasn't pulling my weight. I don't understand! I have been working hard ever since I got here. I suppose I've been a bit slow but I've been trying hard to pick things up! I've done everything that I've been asked to do.  The people I work with haven't been particularly helpful either. And the training that I received wasn't great. No one showed me how to order paper.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le09ob11re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: You mustn't blame your coworkers. I understand that you've been put with one of the best teams. Sometimes you ought to be more proactive. Maybe you need to take the initiative and ask what you can do instead of waiting for people to tell you what to do. I imagine you've worked hard at the tasks you've been given but you should do more than just the minimum. You've got to work to pitch in wherever you can.", "id": 2, "time": "33000", "image": "engenn10le09ob11re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: You're right. My editor asked whether I thought my job was a good fit for me or not. I promised him that I would work harder. But how about you? How was your second week?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Great! My editor asked if I wanted to work on editing a whole book. It's a lot of responsibility but I think I should show some confidence and take on the challenge.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Of course! You've got to accept more responsibility when it's offered to you. Congratulations! You must have really impressed him.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Thanks! I just don't want to get in over my head.", "id": 3, "time": "56800", "image": "engenn10le09ob11re2img07.jpg"}]}}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express necessity, duty, and advice. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about my work responsibilities."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about solving problems."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Have you ever felt like you were in over your head? What happened?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What are some things you can do when you are in an overwhelming situation?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name"